<.shell title="Qualification list" current={:qualification_list}>
  <h1>Qualification list</h1>
  <p class="lead">A member's qualifications, grouped by when they expire.</p>

  <h3>On a member's own page</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <.qualification_list
      id="qualification-list-demo"
      groups={SampleData.qualification_groups()}
      timezone="America/Vancouver"
    />
  </div>

  <h3>On a team admin's member page</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <.qualification_list
      id="qualification-list-admin-demo"
      groups={SampleData.qualification_groups()}
      timezone="America/Vancouver"
      href={fn _qualification -> "#" end}
      earlier={true}
    >
      <:action>
        <.button type="button" variant={:link}>Remove</.button>
      </:action>
    </.qualification_list>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    The qualifications one member holds and has held, on their own page and on a team admin's member page.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    Many members' awards of one qualification. Use a <a href={page_path(:table)}>table</a>, as on a qualification's page.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul class="list">
    <li>
      Groups come in this order: expiring within 60 days, within 180 days, later, does not expire, and expired. An empty group does not show. 60 days is the same window as the team's expiring qualifications.
    </li>
    <li>
      Each group is a heading over a table, one row per qualification, from its latest award. A renewed one stays in its current group, with the year it was first held. Team admins also see each earlier award in its own column.
    </li>
    <li>
      Expired ones are history, not a problem: the heading is muted, and the Held column says when the member held it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.qualification_list id groups timezone href earlier&gt;</code>
    with groups from <code>MemberRecords.group_awards/2</code>. An optional
    <code>&lt;:action :let=&#123;award&#125;&gt;</code>
    goes after each award, such as Remove on a team on SAR Duty Records.
  </p>
</.shell>
